 b|^2 = |a|^2 + |b|^2 + 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$$", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 2}, {"id": "stream:practice-b65fdf71-e094-47b9-a988-84b22fbf19bc", "role": "assistant", "text": "{\"questions\": [{\"question\": \"Two paths have amplitudes $1/2$ and $e^{i\\\\phi}/2$. Find $P(\\\\phi)$ and when it is zero.\", \"origin\": \"self_created\", \"source_refs\": []}]}", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 3}, {"id": "stream-user:branch:cross-term", "role": "user", "text": "Why is the cross term 2 Re(a* b)?", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 4}, {"id": "stream:branch:cross-term", "role": "assistant", "text": "Because $|z|^2 = z^* z$, the cross terms give $2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$.\n<teaching-decision>{\"depth\": \"short\", \"category\": \"local\", \"rationale\": \"Local algebra\", \"suggest_supplement\": false, \"supplement_goal\": \"\"}</teaching-decision>", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 5}, {"id": "stream-user:reply:cross-term:06caad68-8d32-4206-8f8a-44629d919768", "role": "user", "text": "And when both amplitudes are real?", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 6}, {"id": "stream:reply:cross-term:06caad68-8d32-4206-8f8a-44629d919768", "role": "assistant", "text": "## Adding path amplitudes\n\nEach path carries a complex amplitude $a$ or $b$.\n\n$$P = |a + b|^2 = |a|^2 + |b|^2 + 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$$", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f9