id": "states", "sources": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2", "id": "line-2", "locator": {"line": 2}, "text": "Two paths reach the same detector, each with a complex amplitude.", "stale": false}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3", "id": "line-3", "locator": {"line": 3}, "text": "The total amplitude is the sum of the path amplitudes.", "stale": false}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4", "id": "line-4", "locator": {"line": 4}, "text": "The probability is the squared magnitude of the total amplitude.", "stale": false}]}, "active_branch": null, "due_explanations": [], "unanswered_questions": [], "recent_interactions": [{"id": "stream:practice-b65fdf71-e094-47b9-a988-84b22fbf19bc", "role": "assistant", "text": "{\"questions\": [{\"question\": \"Two paths have amplitudes $1/2$ and $e^{i\\\\phi}/2$. Find $P(\\\\phi)$ and when it is zero.\", \"origin\": \"self_created\", \"source_refs\": []}]}", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 3}, {"id": "stream-user:branch:cross-term", "role": "user", "text": "Why is the cross term 2 Re(a* b)?", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 4}, {"id": "stream:branch:cross-term", "role": "assistant", "text": "Because $|z|^2 = z^* z$, the cross terms give $2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$.\n<teaching-decision>{\"depth\": \"short\", \"category\": \"local\", \"rationale\": \"Local algebra\", \"suggest_supplement\": false, \"supplement_goal\": \"\"}</teaching-decision>", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 5}, {"id": "stream-user:reply:cross-term:06caad68-8d32-4206-8f8a-44629d919768", "role": "user", "text": "And when both amplitudes are real?", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 6}, {"id": "stream:reply:cross-term:06caad68-8d32-4206-8f8a-44629d919768", "role": "assistant", "text": "## Adding path amplitudes\n\nEach path carries a complex amplitude $a$ or $b$.\n\n$$P = |a + b|^2 = |a|^2 + |b|^2 + 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(a^* b)$$", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 7}, {"id": "stream:practice-936974b2-f7cc-4ae7-892d-6f910779519d", "role": "assistant", "text": "{\"feedback\": \"Expand $|z|^2 = z^* z$ first.\"}", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 8}, {"id": "practice-feedback:practice-936974b2-f7cc-4ae7-892d-6f910779519d", "role": "assistant", "text": "Expand $|z|^2 = z^* z$ first.", "concept_id": "paths", "supplied_source_refs": [], "source_refs": [], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 9}, {"id": "practice-answer:practice-3fdaffd6-293e-4f4e-8113-bd5559607280", "role": "user", "text": "P = (1 + cos phi)/2, zero at phi = 0.", "concept_id": "paths", "source_refs": [{"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-2"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-3"}, {"source_id": "src-f571a64fdf00f099656a6c50", "revision": "363a18ff401bcf835bdf439f1d8372e9245ab8e8fcbec5a2f941d2a8789e7645", "unit_id": "line-4"}], "source_context_concept_id": "paths", "sequence": 10}]}, "language": "en", "learner_profile": {"goal": "Understand interference and measurement", "depth": "standard", "prerequisites": [{"topic": "Complex numbers", "level": "some"}], "focus": "Problem solving"}}, "attempt": 1, "status": "completed", "text": "{\"feedback\": \"$P(\\\\phi)$ is right; check when the cosine is $-1$.\", \"outcome\": \"needs_work\"}", "final_text": "{\"feedback\": \"$P(\\\\phi)$ is right; check when the cosine is $-1$.\", \"outcome\": \"needs_work\"}", "sequence": 3, "started_at": 1795105973.8576322, "metrics": {"first_delta_s": 0.007785797119140625, "full_s": 0.018590927124023438, "save_s": 0.00014745500084245577}, "attempts": [], "resume_requests": []}');
